DEFINITION  Koerneria pararmatus genome assembly, organelle: mitochondrion.
ACCESSION   OZ057411
VERSION     OZ057411.1
KEYWORDS    .
SOURCE      mitochondrion Allodiplogaster pararmata
  ORGANISM  Allodiplogaster pararmata
            Eukaryota; Metazoa; Ecdysozoa; Nematoda; Chromadorea; Rhabditida;
            Rhabditina; Diplogasteromorpha; Diplogasteroidea; Diplogasteridae;
            Allodiplogaster.
REFERENCE   1
  CONSRTM   Wellcome Sanger Tree of Life Programme
  TITLE     Direct Submission
  JOURNAL   Submitted (16-MAY-2024) WELLCOME SANGER INSTITUTE, Tree of Life,
            Wellcome Genome Campus, Hinxton CB10 1SA, United Kingdom
COMMENT     The assembly nxAllPara2.1 is based on PacBio HiFi derived from a
            single male individual using the Picogram Input Multimodal
            Sequencing (PiMmS) method which was scaffolded using Hi-C data
            derived from a pool of 40 individuals. This genome was generated by
            the Single Nematode Genomes study within the Wellcome Sanger
            Institute's 959 Nematode Genomes project. The assembly process
            included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly
            generation with hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with
            purge_dups, contamination removal via blobtoolkit, and scaffolding
            with YaHS. Bipartite mitochondrial genomes were identified using
            Mitohifi (15.3 kb mitochondrial genome with 7 PCG including Cox2)
            and tblastn (14.6 kb mitochondrial genome with 6 unidirectional PCG
            including Cox1).
